{
 "dur": 65.5,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "How do you dig a subway tunnel",
    "without tearing up the city?",
    "You send in a",
    "tunnel boring machine."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 5.78,
   "chunks": [
    "Think of it as",
    "a factory on rails:",
    "a giant drill up front,",
    "and a moving construction site behind it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 11.64,
   "chunks": [
    "The cutterhead spins",
    "a few times a minute.",
    "Steel disc cutters press into the rock",
    "until it cracks and chips away."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 17.81,
   "chunks": [
    "In soft ground,",
    "pressurized soil or slurry",
    "holds up the face,",
    "so the earth doesn't collapse."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 23.56,
   "chunks": [
    "Behind the cutterhead,",
    "a steel shield",
    "keeps the tunnel open",
    "while the crew works inside."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 28.64,
   "chunks": [
    "The broken rock, called muck,",
    "is scooped up,",
    "carried back by a screw conveyor,",
    "then belted out of the tunnel."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 34.77,
   "chunks": [
    "Now the clever part.",
    "A robotic arm sets",
    "curved concrete segments into a ring,",
    "building the tunnel lining as it goes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 41.82,
   "chunks": [
    "Hydraulic rams push off",
    "that fresh ring",
    "to shove the whole machine forward.",
    "Adjust the rams, and it steers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 47.98,
   "chunks": [
    "Cut, muck, ring, push.",
    "Repeat, around the clock."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 52.7,
   "chunks": [
    "New York's Second Avenue Subway machine",
    "was 450 feet long,",
    "and averaged about 60 feet a day",
    "under Manhattan."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 60.27,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "the tunnel boring machine."
   ]
  }
 ]
}